# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fork ownership. Keep this block last: CODEOWNERS resolves by last match, and
# the entries above name upstream Twenty maintainers who are not collaborators
# here. Append to it rather than editing it in place, so an upstream sync
# conflicts at the end of the file or not at all.
#
# These are the paths a rollback does not undo. Everything else deploys and
# reverts on its own, so it does not need the production owner in the loop.
# See deploy/TEAM-WORKFLOW.md, "What needs the production owner".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Migrations, upgrade commands, and entities are deliberately absent. Once one
# has run against production the previous image does not un-run it, but the
# thing that makes that safe is a staging deploy somebody exercised, not a
# second pair of eyes on the diff. So they are gated at promotion instead of at
# merge: ci-fork-release-risk labels them `risk:database`, and
# deploy-production.yml refuses them until staging-signoff.yml has signed off a
# staging deploy containing them. See deploy/TEAM-WORKFLOW.md.

# Access control: bad state outlives the rollback in sessions and tokens.
